---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field expected_project_id? number Optional. The project_id from the rules being changed. The update is rejected when it does not match the current project, so a change never lands in a project the user did not look at.
---@field marketing_frequency_cap_max_messages? number|distilled.Null The most marketing messages one person gets in the window, across all workflows and broadcasts. Set it together with marketing_frequency_cap_window_days, or set both to null to turn the cap off. Transactional messages are never capped. The recommended cap is 1 message every 2 days.
---@field marketing_frequency_cap_window_days? number|distilled.Null The length of the rolling frequency cap window, in days. Set it together with marketing_frequency_cap_max_messages, or set both to null to turn the cap off.
---@field marketing_frequency_cap_hold_hours? number|distilled.Null How many hours a marketing message over the frequency cap waits for a free slot before it is skipped. Null skips it right away. A held message sends as soon as one of the person's earlier messages leaves the window.
---@field email_tracking_consent_mode? posthog.workflow_sending_rules.EmailTrackingConsentModeEnum|string Whether tracking opens and clicks on marketing email needs the recipient's consent. 'off' follows each email step's own setting, 'opt_out' tracks unless the recipient objected, and 'opt_in' tracks only recipients who consented. Transactional email is never affected. * `off` - Off * `opt_out` - Opt Out * `opt_in` - Opt In
---@field capture_workflows_engagement_events? boolean Capture email sends, opens, clicks and bounces as PostHog events, so they can be used in insights and funnels. These events count toward the project's event usage.

